  "details": "Typing indicator of Chatbox feature does not show up while solely composing in Japanese IME (Input Method Editor https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Input_method).\n\nSee last half of this movie (from 0:23). https://twitter.com/naqtn/status/1558893593657769984 From 0:34, I typed ASCII characters via IME. No typing indicator appears.\n\nEven if with Japanese characters, the indicator shows up after IME has done its job. (The movie doesn't demonstrates this. oops)\n\nI tested with 2022.2.2p3 build 1222\n\n\n# imo\nThere are another IME issues.\n- https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/no-clauses-indications-on-japanese-ime-text\n- https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/japanese-input-issue\n(also I found others not described those posts)\n\nThough I don't know what component the client use for input, Unity InputField is historically buggy in this point. Actually, poor handling of IME is very common thing among PC games using Unity. And \"copy and paste\" is well-know workaround for gamers.\nSo I don't expect this will be fixed sooner. But at least, I want VRChat dev team know this issues as known-bugs.\nI don't know deeper level of technical aspects, but TMP_InputField might do better job than InputField.",
